WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:06.060
When I tell you to think about the words “bravery”
and “One Piece”, the chances are high

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:12.370
that a certain character just appeared before
your eyes: Usopp. But why is that? I was thinking

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:17.199
about this a lot when I was rereading the
entire story the other day. How is it that

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:22.921
in a world which is buzzing with brave characters
facing the most unthinkable situations, our

00:00:22.921 --> 00:00:28.660
mind still moves to someone that often is
undeniably afraid? What makes Usopp a true

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.510
symbol of bravery for us?
To answer this question, we must first understand

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:39.430
what it actually means to be brave. Bravery
is the admirable quality of being able to

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:44.539
confront frightening things. And since everyone
is afraid of different things, being brave

00:00:44.539 --> 00:00:50.700
means something different for every one of
us. To Illustrate this, imagine two very different

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.879
characters: A knight that is used to being
on the battlefield and a small boy who is

00:00:55.879 --> 00:01:01.570
rather shy and has difficulties making friends.
Clearly, both of them have very different

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:06.430
fears. It might take bravery for the knight
to battle a dragon instead of regular people,

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:11.900
but it also takes bravery for the shy child
to walk into a new classroom meeting new people.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.580
A very common misconception about bravery
is that being brave equals not being afraid.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:23.790
This is simply not true though. Brave people
DO feel fear, but they are able to manage

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:28.770
and overcome this fear so that it does not
stop them from taking action. They have trained

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:34.020
themselves to manage their emotional response
to being afraid. As a result, they overcome

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:39.399
their fear rather than the fear overcoming
them. You could even say that in a way, one

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:45.689
cannot be brave without being afraid. It is
important to understand this, since Usopp

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:51.969
is often criticized for still being a coward
and afraid in certain situations. As we now

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:57.430
know, this argument is not really valid. In
order to be brave, you do not have to lose

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:02.500
your fear, but much rather learn how to manage
and overcome it. What we have to look for

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:07.360
in Usopp´s development as a character then,
is not whether he becomes less and less afraid

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.690
over time, but rather if he becomes more and
more able to deal with his anxiety. And that

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:17.390
is exactly what we will do in this video.
We will look at the most important moments

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:22.390
in Usopp´s character arc and try to understand
whether he truly hasn´t developed at all

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:27.710
over time or if he maybe is closer to his
dream than we all tend to think.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:33.570
We first get to meet Usopp in Syrup Village
back in the East Blue. He is a cowardly and

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:37.970
chronically lying young man that struggles
growing up without his parents. While the

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:42.980
villagers all blame Usopp for this behavior,
apparently none of them had the idea to take

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.821
the orphaned boy in and give him the love
and attention he clearly is looking for. Maybe

00:02:47.821 --> 00:02:53.170
this was due to his father being a pirate.
Still, this is no real excuse to abandon a

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:58.720
lonely child in my mind. As a matter of fact,
Usopp started his habit of lying in the first

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:03.360
place, when he started yelling to his sick
mother that pirates were coming, hoping that

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.790
the thought of her husband returning would
strengthen her spirits enough to keep her

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:12.790
alive. It is truly astonishing then, that
despite his understandable lack of confidence

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:18.550
and need for attention, Usopp still grew up
to be a compassionate, extroverted and selfless

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.650
man.
Based on his backstory, I would say that we

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:26.560
have a relatively good idea as to WHY Usopp
turned out to be such a cowardly and anxious

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:31.510
person when he first encounters Luffy and
Zoro. In other words, the starting point for

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:37.000
Usopp´s character arc is a lying coward,
whose insecurity and deep lack of self-confidence

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.720
are rooted in a lack of love and attention
he received while growing up.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:46.510
In essence, similar to all the straw hats,
Usopp´s character arc consists of two major

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:52.160
parts: His relationship with Luffy and his
dream. Especially in Usopp´s case, these

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.470
two themes are very closely interconnected,
as we will see over the course of his journey.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:04.540
Usopp´s relationship with Luffy starts of
as a mix of admiration, friendship and defiance.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:09.180
Luffy safes Usopp´s village from the evil
captain Kuro, who was trying to kill his dear

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:15.230
childhood friend Kaya for her family´s fortune.
Usopp admires Luffy for his strength and decides

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:20.220
to set out to see with him to become a pirate
like his father. The friendship he develops

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:26.180
with Luffy is different from the other straw
hats. Both are two young men around the same

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:30.710
age, with similar interests and a similar
sort of humor. While this friendship plays

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:36.460
an important role in creating the early dynamic
of the crew, it also causes Usopp to continuously

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:41.310
underestimate Luffy´s authority as a captain.
Especially in the early days of the crew,

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:47.090
we often see him trying to compete with Luffy
over the role as captain. This is the starting

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:52.680
point Usopp´s relationship with Luffy.
In comparison, Usopp doesn´t find his dream

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:58.540
and ambition until the events at Arlong Park.
Only when one of Arlong´s fishman, Chu, is

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:04.030
shooting water bullets at Usopp, who is hiding
behind a tree, does he realize that he wants

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:10.890
to help his friends. He decides to become
“a brave warrior of the sea”. In other

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:16.760
words: Usopp dreams of overcoming his fear
and insecurity. In this moment, for the first

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:21.660
time, he goes on to overcome his cowardness
and actually manages to outwit and defeat

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:27.270
the fishman by himself.
This dream Usopp found for himself, is cemented

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:30.880
further on Little Garden after entering the
Grand Line, where he meets the two giants

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:36.480
Dorry and Brogy. After learning about their
ever-lasting battle on the island, Usopp takes

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.650
the giants of Elbaf as a role model for his
ambitions. A theme that reappears throughout

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:46.040
the entire series.
The next big obstacle he has to overcome,

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:52.900
is in Alabasta, where together with Chopper
he has to fight Mr. 4 and Ms. Merry Christmas.

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:58.670
For the first time, Usopp´s loyalty towards
Luffy is put to the test. Usopp raises to

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:04.360
the challenge, and that in a fight where he
even takes a hammer to the head. Nonetheless,

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:10.330
Usopp overcomes his pain, proclaims Luffy
as the future pirate king and ultimately manages

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:16.050
to defeat the two agents together with Chopper.
Battles like this continue to progress Usopp´s

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:20.740
dream to become a brave warrior of the sea.
But with every arc, his insecurity about his

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:26.400
role in the crew grows worse, slowly but steadily.
The reader already starts to get a feeling

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.960
that these negative emotions might end up
in disaster.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:36.490
What follows next, is one of two decisive
turning points in Usopp’s character development:

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:42.660
The Water 7 and Ennis Lobby arc marked a low
and at the same time turning point for Usopp.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:46.520
After the straw hats learn that the Going
Merry won´t be able to continue her journey

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:52.720
due to irreparable damage, Luffy decides to
leave the ship behind. This is a breaking

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:58.300
point for Usopp for several reasons: Obviously,
the Merry was a fond memory of his village

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:02.500
and his friends. But of course, it goes much
deeper than this.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:06.800
Usopp´s feeling that he doesn´t have a role
in the crew has slowly been building up in

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:12.570
him over time. Even though Sanji calls him
the straw hats sniper in Alabasta, Usopp is

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:17.680
not able to identify with this position yet.
In the Merry he sees a crew member that has

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:22.700
grown too weak and as a result was abandoned
by the crew. Not only does he see himself

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:27.210
as one of the weakest members on the ship,
he also doesn´t feel like he has another

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:33.630
purpose to fulfill, like Nami or Chopper do.
As a result, Usopp is afraid to be left behind

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:39.120
by his comrades, just like the merry was.
Luffy even goes so far as to tell him that

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.970
he is not a shipwright, after he unsuccessfully
tries to fight for the Merry´s remain.

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:48.930
Usopp then goes on to openly confront Luffy
with his anxiety: “You can just cut off

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:54.160
those members that are useless. There's no
way I could catch up to you monsters, you

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:59.740
don't need any weak members, right Luffy?”
This anxiety of not being good enough and

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:04.340
being left behind combined with his lack of
respect for Luffy´s position culminate in

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:09.820
his decision to leave the crew and ultimately
fightLuffy for the ownership of the merry.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:15.650
This marks the absolute low point in Usopp´s
story arc. Not only was he unable to act according

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:20.220
to his dream, but he also broke his ties with
Luffy, which removed him from the crew on

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:24.470
an ideological level as well.
After instantly regretting his decision to

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:30.930
break with the crew, Usopp creates the character
of “Sogeking” for himself. He is a representation

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:36.159
of everything Usopp wants to be and at this
point in the story serves as a source of courage

00:08:36.159 --> 00:08:40.860
for him. Hiding behind a mask gives him the
opportunity to fight besides his forsaken

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:46.700
friends and gives him a feeling of security
during the battle on Ennis Lobby. After almost

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:52.779
being killed by Jabra, Sanji safes Usopp and
tells him: “Do what only you can do!”

00:08:52.779 --> 00:08:58.480
Finally, Usopp accepts and establishes his
role and purpose in the crew and starts sniping

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.330
towards the gates of justice to protect Robin.
When the crew is about to leave him behind

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:08.790
back at water 7, he finally demonstrates bravery
and manages to overcome his fear of being

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:15.010
left behind and not fitting in. He apologizes
to Luffy and the crew and fully accepts Luffy

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:20.279
as the captain. This entire arc of redemption
was of great importance to the development

00:09:20.279 --> 00:09:26.310
of Usopp in regard to both his dream AND his
relationship with Luffy. Usopp has now officially

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:31.110
rejoined the crew after an incredible 106
chapters of absence.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:36.880
Our next stop is Thriller bark, where Usopp
once again has to rely on Sogeking in order

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:41.990
to fight Perona. It is the first situation
though, in which he is the only one capable

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:47.360
of defeating an enemy. This time, he has to
overcome his anxiety to fight for the sake

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:52.279
of the entire crew.
After the events of Marineford, Usopp desperately

00:09:52.279 --> 00:09:56.780
tries to get back to Luffy, saying that if
he cannot comfort his captain in times like

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:02.370
this, he could not call himself a true straw
hat. This shows us that his acceptance and

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:07.940
relationship with Luffy has gone full circle.
Over the course of the two years, Usopp then

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:13.649
tries to get as strong as he can for his captain
and aims to become a true sniper, worthy of

00:10:13.649 --> 00:10:18.520
fighting for the future pirate king.
The last arc that we have to look in order

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:24.779
to understand Usopp´s character development
is Dressrosa. This is the second major turning

00:10:24.779 --> 00:10:29.830
point for Usopp in the story so far. When
stuck in the underground harbor, Robin gets

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:36.070
turned into a toy, leaving Usopp as the last
remaining straw hat against Trebol and Sugar.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:41.400
The Tontatta, who are being wiped out by Trebol,
put all their hopes in Usolando, another character

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:47.320
created by Usopp to hide behind. This puts
immense stress on Usopp that has been building

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:52.770
up for the majority of the arc. Finally, he
can´t handle it anymore and, as he did at

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:58.540
Arlong Park, he runs away to hide.
Tragically, right here Usopp represents one

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:04.240
of the main themes of Dressrosa: Deception.
All this time Doflamingo had been deceiving

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:09.290
the Tontatta and now they have to find out
that Usopp was essentially doing the same.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:15.020
Yet, as he did at Arlong Park, Usopp realizes
that this is not who he wants to be. He comes

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:20.970
out and tells the Tontatta´s the truth. He
is Usopp, the sniper of the Straw hat pirates.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:26.820
And he will be their hero. In this moment,
having neither Sogeking nor Usolando left

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:32.280
to hide behind, he finally overcomes another
one of his great insecurities and stands against

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:38.089
Trebol and Sugar as himself. He no longer
needs a mask to hide behind.

00:11:38.089 --> 00:11:43.960
He successfully saves the Tontatta and even
manages to knock out Sugar twice. His newly

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:48.980
found courage and self-confidence are almost
directly rewarded by the awakening of his

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:55.500
observation Haki, that he uses to safe Luffy
and Law. Finally, he was able to prove his

00:11:55.500 --> 00:12:01.580
worth for Luffy, not to the others, but to
himself and confirm his right for being part

